      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "§6Rich Mineral Deposits§r generate on §6Ike§r and §6Moho§r, between Y 12 and 44. They are a source of rare light metals.\n\nFirst turn the ore into §6Mineral Dust§r:\n- The simple way: crystallize the ore in the §3Ore Acidizer§r, then centrifuge the crystals into 2 dust plus iron, aluminium and lithium.\n- The better way: dissolve the ore in nitric acid in the §3Industrial Mixer§r, separate the solution in the §3Gas Centrifuge§r, and shred the cleaned crystals into 4 dust.\n\nThen acidize the dust and centrifuge the fragments. The acid decides what you get:\n- Peroxide (default) - mostly niobium, plus cobalt, zirconium, beryllium.\n- Nitric acid - mostly gallium, plus beryllium, niobium, lanthanum.\n- Sulfuric acid - mostly beryllium, plus niobium, gallium, lanthanum.\n- Solvent - mostly cobalt, plus gallium, niobium, coltan.\n- Hydrochloric acid - mostly zirconium, plus neodymium, niobium, cobalt.\n- Schrabidic acid - cobalt-60, bismuth, technetium and asbestos.",
